on  zuckerberg apologized publicly and the  student paper ran articles stating that  his site was completely improper  in 2003 zuckerberg met his now wife  priscilla chan waiting in line for the  bathroom at a frat party thrown by  zuckerberg's fraternity alpha epsilon  pie during zuckerberg's sophomore year  he met eduardo saverin a junior at  harvard in late 2003 he asked eduardo to  deposit fifteen thousand dollars in a  bank account that would be accessible to  both of them the money zuckerberg  promised would go toward the servers  needed to host a site he wanted to  develop  the following semester in january 2004  zuckerberg began writing code for a new  website with his friends out of his dorm  room on february 4th 2004 zuckerberg  launched the facebook later changing the  name to facebook six days after the site  launched three harvard seniors cameron  winklevoss tyler winklevoss and divya  narendra accused zuckerberg of  intentionally misleading them into  believing he would help them build a  social network called  harvardconnection.com while zuckerberg  was instead using their ideas to build  facebook the three complained to the  harvard crimson and the newspaper began  an investigation while zuckerberg tried  to convince the editors not to run the  story he broke into two of the editors  email accounts he did it based on the  editor's private login details from  facebook  the winklevoss twins would eventually  reach a settlement and received 20  million dollars in cash and the rest of  the 65 million dollars in stock in  february 2008.  in june 2004 zuckerberg ran into sean  parker an internet startup kid best  known for co-founding napster parker  soon joined facebook  his first task was to do one of the  things eduardo was supposed to do but  hadn't yet help facebook source funding  parker had raised money for napster and  he knew his way around silicon valley he  quickly proved himself capable for  zuckerberg this only reinforced the idea  that eduardo was expendable  in the middle of that summer zuckerberg  planned to oust his co-founder eduardo  in december 2004 zuckerberg dropped out  of harvard after his sophomore year to  focus on facebook full-time  he wasn't the most polished businessman  in facebook's early days he carried  business cards that read a little  something like this  on january 7th 2005 zuckerberg caused  facebook to issue 9 million shares of  common stock in a company he took 3.3  million shares for himself and gave 2  million shares to sean parker he also  gave dustin moskowitz a co-founder of  facebook 2 million shares this instantly  diluted eduardo's stake in the company  from around 24 percent to below 10  eduardo only found out how badly he'd  been diluted a few months later  zuckerberg even fired eduardo for not  complying the conflict ultimately ended  in 2009 when lawsuits were settled out  of court  in 2010 time magazine named mark  zuckerberg person of the year  on may 18 2012 zuckerberg took facebook  public the ipo raised 16 billion dollars  making it the biggest tech ipo in  history at the time  zuckerberg became the 29th richest  person on the planet overnight  aside from his philanthropic work he  also loves to spend he reportedly bought  the pagani huayra for around 1.4 million  dollars he also likes to spend his money  on privacy in 2011 zuckerberg reportedly  bought his  5600 square foot home in palo alto  california for 7 million  and then spent an additional 45 million  dollars on the four houses in the land  around it for the sake of privacy in  october 2014 he shelled out around 100  million dollars for 700 acres of  secluded land on a hawaiian island  zuckerberg hasn't been afraid to spend  facebook's money either the company had  some major acquisitions under its belt  including 1 billion dollars for  instagram  19 billion dollars for whatsapp and 2  billion for oculus facebook's family of  apps is used by more than 3 billion  people each month in 2021 the company  reported a revenue of more than 117  billion dollars  in march 2018 it was revealed data  analytics company cambridge analytica  harvested data from over 50 million  facebook users profiles a number  facebook later said was closer to 87  million and used it to target voters  during the 2016 election zuckerberg was  called on to appear in front of  lawmakers in two testimonies that lasted  five hours each  ahead of the testimonies facebook  reportedly hired a team of experts to  coach zuckerberg on how to answer  congress's questions and how to be  charming in 2018 facebook also faced  accusations that its moderation efforts  weren't adequate in stopping the spread  of hate speech and disinformation on its  network  reports revealed that facebook was used  to incite genocide against the muslim  minority in myanmar by the country's  military officials in september 2018  instagram co-founders kevin systrom and  mike krieger abruptly announced they  were leaving facebook it was later  reported they had left amid growing  tensions with zuckerberg and that the  pair were fighting with facebook  leadership over instagram's autonomy the  departure of instagram's co-founders was  quickly followed by scathing remarks  from whatsapp co-founder brian acton who  detailed disagreements with facebook  executives over user privacy both  whatsapp co-founders had left the  company earlier that year in september  2018 facebook announced it had been  hacked around 30 million users had their  personal information compromised making  it the worst hack in facebook's 15-year  history  facebook spent around 23 million dollars  on personal security for zuckerberg and  his family in october 2019 zuckerberg  was once again called on to testify in  front of congress this time about  facebook's plans for its libra digital  currency  congressional members also grilled him  on the company's content moderation  practices despite the backlash  zuckerberg has defended facebook's  positions on freedom of speech  describing the platform's role as a  place where users can share a diversity  of viewpoints zuckerberg testified  before congress yet again in 2020  alongside tim cook jeff bezos and sundar  pichai over matters of antitrust  facebook was later hit with two  anti-trust suits that seek to break up  the company  on april 3rd 2021 facebook experienced  yet another major data breach this time  533 million facebook users had their  data leaked online the league included  their phone numbers facebook ids full  names locations birthdates bios and  email addresses raising serious  questions about user privacy  on october 28 2021 facebook was renamed  meta the move reflected the company's  growing ambitions beyond social media  meta is based on the sci-fi term  metaverse to describe its vision for  working and playing in a virtual world  zuckerberg sees the metaverse as the  next frontier and an integral part of  web 3. his plan is that within the next  decade the metaverse will reach more  than a billion users host hundreds of  billions of dollars of digital commerce  and support jobs for millions of  creators and developers  he also plans to spend billions over the  next few years developing the  technologies required for building the  metaverse while the metaverse can  elevate existing social media  experiences and open new opportunities  for businesses with the adaptation of  cryptocurrencies blockchain games  decentralized finance nfts and  tokenization of content  but not everyone is on board with the  metaverse meta has been met with huge  criticism meta's dependence on vr  technology has limited development and  wide scale adoption limitations of  portable hardware and the need to  balance cost and design have caused a  lack of high quality graphics and  mobility  there are also concerns over user  addiction the metaverse has also been  described as dystopian and experts are  concerned that the metaverse could be  used as an escape from reality in a  similar fashion to existing internet  technologies  on february the 3rd 2022 facebook's  parent company meta platforms plunged 26  and it raised more than 230 billion  dollars in market cap it's the biggest  wipeout for any u.s company ever and the  one day crash now ranks as the worst in  stock market history zuckerberg saw 30  billion dollars wiped from his net worth  analysts pointed to the stiff  competition from other social media  platforms and lower than expected  revenues mata's dismal quarterly  earnings report showed declining users  and surging expenses related to the  company's metaverse project but  zuckerberg plans to invest more in the  metaverse project and is shifting more  of meta's resources into making the  project a success  there's a lesson in every story what can  we learn from mark zuckerberg's journey  he's for sure had a lot of ups and downs  there's still speculation as to whether  he stole the idea from the winklevoss  twins and the way he backstabbed his  business partner eduardo has raised  questions about his morality and ethics  facebook's various scandals have also  drawn a lot of criticism over the years  but without mark zuckerberg facebook  probably wouldn't exist his genius lies  in his ability to look towards the  future he recognized the internet was  growing at a rapid pace and decided to  capitalize on it facebook is still the  most popular social media site and has  over 2 billion monthly active users  along with the acquisition of other  social media giants such as whatsapp and  instagram meta has dominated social  media there's no doubt he's built  something remarkable that has made both  positive and negative impacts on our  lives what do you guys think is the  metaverse here to stay or is it just an  overhyped fantasy the comment section in  this one will be very interesting  thanks for staying till the end of this  video if you enjoyed this video then be  sure to hit the like button drop a  comment subscribe and hit the  notification bell for more content like  this  also be sure to check out our other  videos on this channel links are in the  description and we'll see you in the  next one

